[Unit]
Description=Private network for WordPress staging + its database

[Network]
# The ONE exception to host networking in this stack: the official
# wordpress image hardcodes Apache to port 80 with no env var to change it,
# and rootless Podman can't reliably bind privileged (<1024) host ports
# under host networking without a host-wide sysctl change. A private bridge
# + PublishPort= sidesteps that entirely via rootlessport, the same proven
# mechanism already serving paperless_default/khoj_default's published
# ports on this host today. WordPress doesn't need to reach Ollama/ComfyUI
# directly anyway -- only the agency's own host-native Python process talks
# to it, via its published port -- so isolating it costs nothing.
